"""Mutations of part 7h's Junkers 88 (src/game/junkers88.*) for ../mutfast.py with the actors build:

    python mutfast.py mutations/mutate_7h.py --models DIR --build build_item.bat --check check_item.py

Each should make check_item.py fail (or the harness crash / hang). Generated from the sources (a
comparison, a number, an operator or a statement per line), then pruned. Left out as equivalent
(98): NormalizeBy's / LengthOf's exact-1 and 1e-8 limits, the sign tests of their degenerate
branches and the assignments there (a tiny component keeps its sign); the chatter bearing's
normalisations and their limits (atan2 does not see the length; a NaN length leaves the heading
unnormalised, the same direction), the bearing's clamps (unreachable or the same); FindTarget's
normalisations of the line and the view (only the dot product's sign is used); a new frame's place
and rotation set to what it has (SetRot normalises); members set again before they are read (the
fighter's flags, smoke, timers, path, health; a path's index, a part's index, the fall's radius,
the debris' w, the groups' counts, the health, rate, hits and slow motion StartMission sets, the
motor's and the guns' ranges set again, the gun cleared); PlayAnimation's result (unused);
a request's w (always 0); short-chunk limits a real chunk cannot reach (RemainingSize > 0 / > 1,
the save id's 0); ties the code never meets (75 % / 25 % exactly: the target is the count left;
the fade's exact 9 s / 11 s; a pause or the slow time exactly 0; the rate exactly 0); a delay
`< 1` on an int; delete loops (leaks: the parts, the debris) and a path's 1023-character limit; the
seat flags' digit (mod 32); EngineFell's return and its search past the start (an engine at stage
0 is always listed); BreakPart's search (the part is always found; from index 0 the same); a
third Advance of an engine (no engine heads a thrown row); reads past a table (undefined: `in`
from -1, m_chatter[-1], OUTER_NAMES[4], DEPENDENT_NAMES[6], wings[2]); the creator's lambda return. 8 more did not
compile (alignas(17), deleted destructors) and were dropped.

Results (2026-10-30): the first run caught 990 of 1,290 run (5 did not compile, 295 survived; 26
header mutations left for the rerun). New cases: the seat flags' file values; LoadSounds with a
file that does not load (released, the rest made, updated, linked keeping nothing) and without a
driver; InitSeats anew (unblocked, flags cleared) and without a dummy; seat 5; the left / right
chatter groups' pauses; level 4 without damage sounds; the damage looks released; a second model
(a two-letter part, a part under a part, the right wing's root before and after its engine,
turned, with a stump; HasNext; Load from a short chunk and onto a shown frame); a model without
blades or engines; the tracers' model not loading; Advance's updates; BreakPart with the part
listed twice; the damage at 0.5 / 0.25, 396 with parts enough, an engine with a stump in its list,
the only engine first, no engine or outer part anywhere, the outer part first (its thrown part
once), the fighters disengaged; debris names (long and found, 255 without an end, empty, one
byte, cut before the length / the floor), exactly 500 m under, two with the first gone; tracers
(ray flags, a hit with height, exactly 1 m, a short chunk, exactly 25 m above, two with the first
spent); the bomber away from the origin along unnormalised, tilted and tiny axes, fighters 15 m up
and 22 m out; the tick's chatter; the update's pauses (1 and 21), the table's end untouched,
slow-motion edges, the damage / debris / propellers / tracers each update, the path's step (time
0, release, two updates) and exact end, the fall's sweep and its update; fighters: their links,
a model that does not load, IsPlaying(0), a shot exactly due, hits to 0.25, the chatter at 0.5,
the attackers counted, PathNote's results, two attacks adding up, a rate of 0.25 left, a path
loaded by its name and a dummy that does not load, the barrels twice as long, the sphere's
centre, the end exactly reached with one smoke finished, everything released, the crash's
direction and flags; FindTarget from elsewhere (views along, across, at right angles, tiny;
nearest by the squares, ties); saved fighters' times, folders and reload, a fighter chunk cut
after its path, the camera and the fall loaded, the velocity, the groups' lists cleared, the
stages' chunk left, empty lists, another first chunk's rest; SetInterceptors. Rerun of the 240:
214 caught (3 did not compile, 23 survived); of the 23, 7 more with new cases (PathNote's early
result, NoPathNote's, the tracers' model cleared first, a steeper axis, a failed path's index, a
tracer and a debris cut short) and 16 equivalent (above). A full rerun: 1,209 of 1,211 caught;
a hit to exactly 0 caught the other, m_chatter[-1] (it had crashed before) dropped: all 1,210 caught."""
